<title>TUNISIA: Rate rises at Tunisian treasury auction.</title>
<headline>Rate rises at Tunisian treasury auction.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tunisian Treasury raised 110 million dinars at its weekly auction of treasury notes and bills dated April 29, and repaid maturing paper totalling 159.2 million dinars.</p>
<p>Rate of the two-year note payable in equal annual tranches rose to 7.0000 percent coupon rate from an average 6.9812 percent last week.</p>
<p>Herewith breakdown of the auction results:</p>
<p> Maturity		    Amount   Rate    Previous week</p>
<p> - 13-week		   10	6.8750   nil</p>
<p>				 20	6.9375   nil</p>
<p> - 26-week		   30	6.9375   nil</p>
<p> - 52-week		   10	6.9375   nil</p>
<p>				 25	7.0000   nil</p>
<p>-Two-year note payable in equal annual tranches</p>
<p>				 15	7.0000    25 MD   6.9375</p>
<p>							 58 MD   7.0000</p>
<p>							average: 6.9812</p>
<p>Banks bid for 383 million dinars for 13-, 26-, 52-week and two-year notes at between 6.8750 and 7.8750 percent.</p>
<p>($1=1.09 dinar)</p>
<p>--Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
</text>
